4) LAUNCH PROFILE
   Accepted: 256 blocks, 1.42 waves/SM, partial wave = 76 blocks (Nsight warning)
   Persistent: 180 blocks, 1.00 waves/SM, zero partial wave (tail eliminated)

   The tail was eliminated but the per-tile scheduling overhead
   (atomicAdd + while loop + __syncthreads) dominates.

5) REASON FOR REJECTION
   - 2.1-2.4x slower across all metrics
   - No resource win (same registers, same shared memory)
   - Dynamic scheduling adds ~300-400k cycles/block of pure overhead
   - Workload imbalance visible in achieved occupancy (78% vs 81%)

